[3] THE PASS-FLIP THRESHOLD (directional risk — the only dangerous direction is TIGHTER):
    theta = 2/(1+y^2)     : banked margin x 19.7 -> budget must tighten below 1.25e-16 m/s^2 to flip
    theta = exp(1-y)      : banked margin x 21.4 -> budget must tighten below 1.15e-16 m/s^2 to flip
    theta = exp((1-y)/2)  : banked margin x 14.0 -> budget must tighten below 1.76e-16 m/s^2 to flip
    flip band: 1.15e-16 .. 1.76e-16 m/s^2 (weakest pass flips first at 1.76e-16)

[4] REACHABILITY of the flip band:
    ideal 20-yr sub-2m Mars analysis (kitchen-sink absorption): a_min ~ 9.1e-17  -> INSIDE the flip band
    15-yr 1.5m Mars, fit-A absorption                         : a_min ~ 1.2e-16  -> INSIDE the flip band
    BepiColombo MORE 1-cm over its 2.5-yr window              : a_min ~ 3.9e-17  -> INSIDE the flip band

VERDICT: CORROBORATED-IN-ORDER + DIRECTIONALLY SAFE TODAY.
  (i) The strict budget sits x4 inside the published per-planet Saturn bound and ~5 orders inside the
      outer-system INPOP exclusion — the right order for a Mars-led differential observable; nothing
      published contradicts it in either direction.
  (ii) The banked M22 passes flip only if the true budget is below 1.2e-16..1.8e-16 m/s^2 — beyond every
